From: Yusuf <yusufyav.dev@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: dw-hdmi-qp: wait up to 2 s for FLT_ready and log it

LTS2 polled SCDC FLT_ready for 400 ms. A BenQ RD280UG coming out of TMDS
was not ready in that time: the first FRL attempt after a hotplug failed
with "sink flt isn't ready" and a later one trained. Poll for up to 2 s
and log how long the sink took, so the figure is measured.
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c
index 20d6a9393..77f001a8e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c
@@ -1982,18 +1982,27 @@ static int dw_hdmi_qp_flt_lts2(struct dw_hdmi_qp *hdmi, u8 rate)
 	u8 val = 0;
 	u8 flt_rate = hdmi_set_frl_mask(rate);
 
-	/* FLT_READY & FFE_LEVELS read */
-	for (i = 0; i < 20; i++) {
+	/*
+	 * FLT_READY & FFE_LEVELS read.
+	 *
+	 * 400 ms was not enough for a BenQ RD280UG coming out of TMDS: the
+	 * first attempt after a hotplug failed and the next one, seconds
+	 * later, trained. Wait up to 2 s and say how long it took, so the
+	 * figure is measured rather than guessed.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < 100; i++) {
 		drm_scdc_readb(hdmi->ddc, SCDC_STATUS_FLAGS_0, &val);
 		if (val & BIT(6))
 			break;
 		msleep(20);
 	}
 
-	if (i == 20) {
-		dev_err(hdmi->dev, "sink flt isn't ready,SCDC_STATUS_FLAGS_0:0x%x\n", val);
+	if (i == 100) {
+		dev_err(hdmi->dev, "sink flt isn't ready after %d ms,SCDC_STATUS_FLAGS_0:0x%x\n",
+			i * 20, val);
 		return LTSL;
 	}
+	dev_info(hdmi->dev, "sink flt ready after %d ms\n", i * 20);
 
 	/* max ffe level 3 */
 	val = hdmi->max_ffe_lv << 4 | flt_rate;
